WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.580
One of the things that was suggested during
the first presidential debate by Donald Trump

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:15.070
was that Trump suggested his supporters go
to the polls and observe what's going on,

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.560
hang out at polling places, see if things
look okay.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:24.929
Now, as I mentioned, if you there are poll
workers and there are poll volunteers, you

00:00:24.929 --> 00:00:28.189
can't just show up and volunteer on the day
off.

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:30.789
You have to actually sign up to do that.

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:35.649
If you just show up and you're, quote, observing
and you're you're essentially loitering in

00:00:35.649 --> 00:00:38.949
some states, that's against the law and it's
voter intimidation.

00:00:38.949 --> 00:00:43.090
And Nevada's attorney general is not taking
this lightly and has said if you do what Trump

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:48.410
is suggesting, we will arrest you and we will
prosecute you because it is in Nevada illegal.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:53.339
Let's start with a reminder about what Donald
Trump said about this Tuesday night at the

00:00:53.339 --> 00:00:54.440
debate.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.770
So I first for you, sir.

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.420
Finally for for the vice president.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.969
I hope neither of you will interrupt the other.

00:01:00.969 --> 00:01:07.420
Will you urge your supporters to stay calm
during this extended period, not to engage

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.189
in any civil unrest?

00:01:09.189 --> 00:01:14.420
And will you pledge tonight that you will
not declare victory until the election has

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.939
been independently certified?

00:01:16.939 --> 00:01:23.020
President Trump, I about watching my supporters
to go into the polls and watch very carefully,

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.260
because that's what has to happen.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.329
I am urging them to do it.

00:01:26.329 --> 00:01:29.230
As you know, today, there was a big problem
in Philadelphia.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:30.310
They went in to watch.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:33.820
They were called poll watchers, a very safe,
very nice thing.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:34.900
They were thrown out.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.380
They weren't allowed to watch.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:37.380
You know why?

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.450
Because bad things happen in Philadelphia.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.450
Bad things.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:47.000
So the reason Trump's poll watchers were thrown
out is that they weren't actually poll watchers.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.180
There is a process.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.960
If you want to be a volunteer, you have to
actually sign up.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.710
Typically, it's run at the county level.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:58.400
But you'd have to see how it is in your your
city, state or municipality.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:05.570
You don't just show up or show up armed as
someone who is there to observe the way Donald

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.899
Trump is suggesting it's not going to do.

00:02:07.899 --> 00:02:12.620
It's voter intimidation to hang out all day
at polls without being an actual volunteer

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:16.110
who signed up and is on a list of someone
who's going to be there to do that.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.280
And Trump is encouraging that.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.480
Trump is encouraging voter intimidation and
it shouldn't surprise us.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.650
Trump encouraged try to vote twice.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.770
That's a felony in some places, including
North Carolina.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:32.200
Trump has encouraged all sorts of behavior
that is either immoral or illegal in some

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.200
cases.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.820
And Nevada's attorney general says we will
prosecute people who do this.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.970
If you do this, we will prosecute, prosecute
you.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:43.849
If you follow Donald Trump's advice and you
go to polling places and you monitor votes

00:02:43.849 --> 00:02:47.710
being cast or counted, it is voter intimidation.

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:55.880
Aaron Ford tweeted, quote, Trump also told
his supporters to go into the polls and watch

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.310
very carefully.

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.920
But he wasn't talking about poll watching.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:02.140
He was talking about voter intimidation.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:06.349
For your information, voter intimidation is
illegal in Nevada.

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:10.530
Believe me when I say it, you do it and you
will be prosecuted.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:17.370
Now, to follow up on Trump's claim that some
injustice has transpired because his fans

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:20.019
who showed up in Philly weren't allowed in.

00:03:20.019 --> 00:03:21.430
We looked into it.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:28.450
Legitimate poll officers and volunteers in
Philadelphia have been able to do their jobs.

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:32.620
But you have to actually be there in an official
capacity.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:37.640
Random people who show up and say I'm going
to watch aren't actually part of anything.

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:40.480
They can't hang out intimidating people.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:41.480
That's not.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:43.560
I was going to say it's not how our democracy
works.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.510
It's not how our democracy is supposed to
work.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:53.140
Now, for you, what to do if you see funny
business when you go to vote?

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.549
Three things to keep in mind.

00:03:54.549 --> 00:04:01.060
Number one, you can report voter intimidation
to the ACLU by calling 866 our vote.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:02.799
Put it in your phone.

00:04:02.799 --> 00:04:08.660
Number two, you can report voter intimidation
or electioneering or whatever to the local

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:10.200
county elections board.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.299
Again, most elections are run at the county
level.

00:04:13.299 --> 00:04:17.040
That's why we get results county by county,
often on election night.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.330
Google the phone number for your county elections
board.

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:22.920
Put it in your phone before you go.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:23.920
You can.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:24.920
Safe.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:28.000
If you can safely and legally get video of
what's going on.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.000
Send it to me.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.520
I will do everything I can to send it to my
media contacts and to publicize it on this

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:34.520
program.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:35.520
This applies to early voting.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:36.520
This applies on Election Day.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:41.400
We will be standing by on Election Day to
hear from you if funny business is going on.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:47.010
It's also important for people to know what
is and is not permitted in their jurisdiction.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:52.170
So there's a brief summary of poll watcher
laws available.

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:57.720
We're linking to a Web site that has that
summary in the description to this YouTube

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:58.720
clip.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:02.781
So you've got already you can just Google
a poll watcher laws, Massachusetts, poll watcher

00:05:02.781 --> 00:05:05.920
laws, Louisiana or whatever state you live
in.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:12.740
So, like as an example, in New York, each
party can have three poll watchers present

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:17.630
and the poll watchers can challenge your right
to vote when you appear at the polling place.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:23.020
But it would not override any anti-discrimination
laws if they're challenging every black voter

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:25.190
or disproportionately black voters.

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:26.330
That wouldn't be OK.

00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:30.020
You know, enforcing it in the heat of Election
Day is another question.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:37.830
It also never permits harassment, intimidation,
coercion, electioneering, trying to either

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.260
prevent someone from voting or influencing
vote.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:41.700
So that's New York.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.180
Understand the laws in your state.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:50.230
And, yeah, it's tragic that this is how we
have to prepare to go and vote.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:56.410
My plan for now is I do have an absentee ballot
coming.

00:05:56.410 --> 00:06:00.600
